  "cites": "a hello that nothing answered before the connection timeout, the default startup posture, a session that started, and a deployment audit log with no record of the unguarded start. The posture is conformant and the silence is not. The step-level twin in acs-f-5 has a Guardian to receive its audit event; here the handshake never completed, so there is no Guardian to receive anything and the deployment's own log is the only witness, which is why the member is SELF. A member that asserted only that the session started would score the default posture as evidence of enforcement.",
